# OPTIONAL: copying this file is no longer required. `docker compose up` works
# with zero config, and Telegram / public URL / identity can all be set in the
# in-app setup wizard after first launch. Use this file only for advanced/static overrides.

# ─── supermux .env ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Copy this file to .env before running `docker compose up`:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# FLOW:
#   1. Set MUX_WEB_PUBLIC_URL to the address where YOUR browser will reach the
#      broker.  For local use, http://localhost:8787 is correct and works as a
#      PWA secure context (localhost is special-cased by browsers).
#      If you expose the broker via a reverse proxy / tunnel, set this to the
#      HTTPS URL you're using instead.
#
#   2. The broker web channel is enabled as soon as MUX_WEB_PORT + MUX_WEB_PUBLIC_URL
#      are both set.  No Telegram token is required to get started.
#
#   3. For Claude authentication: after starting the container run
#        docker compose exec broker claude login
#      and complete the device-flow OAuth in your browser.  Auth is persisted in
#      the `claude-auth` named volume so you only need to do this once.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Port the broker's HTTP server listens on inside the container.
# The compose file maps this to the same port on your host.
MUX_WEB_PORT=8787

# Public URL the browser uses to reach the broker.
# localhost is treated as a secure context by browsers, so the PWA service
# worker and Web Push work correctly without HTTPS.
MUX_WEB_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:8787

# --- Exposing apps (expose_port / Proxies) ---
# MUX_PROXY_BASE_DOMAIN is OPTIONAL.
#   - Set it (e.g. apps.example.com) to give each exposed app its own subdomain:
#     https://<slug>.apps.example.com  — requires wildcard DNS (*.apps.example.com)
#     and a matching wildcard TLS cert (e.g. via Cloudflare).
#   - Leave it UNSET to serve exposed apps under a sub-path on your existing
#     public URL: https://<your-broker>/p/<slug>/  — no wildcard DNS/TLS needed.
#     The proxy strips the /p/<slug> prefix, so this works for apps that use
#     RELATIVE URLs. Apps that assume the site root (absolute /asset paths,
#     fetch('/api'), a root WebSocket, or a framework dev server like Vite/Next)
#     won't work under a sub-path — use subdomain mode for those.
# MUX_PROXY_BASE_DOMAIN=

# Optional — set to enable the Telegram channel.
# Obtain a token from @BotFather on Telegram.
# MUX_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# Optional — override the default state directory inside the container.
# Usually not needed; the named volume at /root/.mux is sufficient.
# MUX_STATE_DIR=/root/.mux/state
